    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working on a 12 week hypertrophy block for a client but they've completely stalled on their squat for the last 3 weeks. progress just stopped. can you explain how deloading or changing the volume/intensity might help them break through this plateau from a physiological standpoint?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prolonged squat stagnation often stems from cumulative microtrauma exceeding the body's capacity for supercompensation, highlighting the need for strategic deloading to allow muscle fibers to fully repair without damage accumulation. Additionally, manipulating volume and intensity can alter mechano-transduction signals, shifting the training stimulus from neural compensation to structural remodeling to bypass plateaus. Implementing these physiological adaptations not only facilitates tissue repair but also creates a fresh mechanical load that re-activates the Hypertrophy Threshold previously reached by the squat.",
